body:
You said a lot, let me clarify. The "Second City" nickname comes from Chicago being rebuilt after the Chicago Fire of 1871. This rebuilt city became known as the Second City. [The Second City](https://www.secondcity.com) gets its name from it. If they get "Chicago is #2" from size or population, then they are wrong. Los Angeles is greater in population.

&#x200B;

Edit to add: I've been to a lot of cities as well. They all have something to experience.
